<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buys 23,000T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buys 23,000T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two South Korean flour mills, Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd and Cheiljedang Corp bought a combined total of 23,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat on Wednesday from a Japanese trading house, Itochu Corp, traders said.  </p>
<p>Details of the tender result are as follows:</p>
<p>Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		4,900   $190.70</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 5,600   $201.35</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  2,500   $206.41</p>
<p>Cheiljedang Corp</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Bushel(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		3,000   $0.55</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		1,300   $0.69</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 2,900   $0.64</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  2,800   $0.96</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
